    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "You were right: this feature should not have existed as a separate runtime module. Lexer-Lux/Lexeditor#130 is explicitly blocked by Lexer-Lux/Lexeditor#126, because camp-rest tonic refill must use the shared DS3-style overflow storage and campsite inventory rather than inventing its own reserve and camp detector. I removed the premature module from the compiled runtime and removed its settings. Lexer-Lux/Lexeditor#130 remains open and blocked by Lexer-Lux/Lexeditor#126; there is nothing to test until that shared storage design is implemented.",
